  "published": "2026-11-06T00:03:49.05Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.4.2 - On SpawnDev.ILGPU.ML 5.8.3 and SpawnDev.ILGPU 5.4.16: faster tensor-core prefill GEMMs and flash prefill (ldmatrix) on the batch decoder, LoRA training steps 2.5x faster (llama3.1:8b 4.5 -> 1.78 s on an RTX 4070). v1.4.1 - AiChatEngine.PassObserver: each generation pass with its exact rendered prompt (token ids and text with special tokens kept), generated token ids, end-of-turn ids, the stop token that ended it, the LoRA adapter label and raw output, for training data that matches inference; AiChatEngine.TokenizeAsync / DecodeAsync; LoRA adapters: ModelRegistry.SetAdapterAsync (PEFT directory or LoraAdapterSet, either engine, swapped in place on the batch decoder). On SpawnDev.ILGPU.ML 5.8.2. v1.4.0 - AiMemoryEngine: memory search on the accelerator (all-MiniLM-L6-v2 + DeviceVectorIndex; 50,000 entries p95 5.6 ms on an RTX 4070 including the embed) and ConsolidateAsync (episodes into facts with provenance, conflicts superseded). OllamaModelInstaller (install a model without Ollama, models.spawndev.com then registry.ollama.ai). AiFaceEngine: face detection and recognition (YuNet + SFace) on the shared accelerator, with a face registry (introductions, Visitor N guests, expiry). Chat on the batch decoder by default (GgufEngine.Auto: qwen2 / qwen3 / llama; llama3.1:8b on an RTX 4070 at a 3.7k-token prompt: first token after 200 new tokens 204 ms, prompt 1,660 tok/s, decode 45.5 tok/s; tensor-core prefill on CUDA sm_75+). Ollama /api/chat and /api/generate report eval_count / eval_duration and the other timing fields. AiSpeakerEngine.ReleaseWorkingMemoryAsync. On SpawnDev.ILGPU.ML 5.8.1 and SpawnDev.ILGPU 5.4.15. v1.3.0 - Live words: AiStreamingSpeechEngine (Nemotron Speech Streaming 0.6B, words as they are spoken, 5.63% WER on 60 LibriSpeech clips, a 160 ms chunk in ~70 ms). Full history: CHANGELOG.md",
